On Saturday, 14 April 2012 20:37:18 UTC-6, ais523  wrote:
> C343-33 Sometimes a monster may remain hidden under a corpse that has
> rotted away.
I've actually already fixed this. The way I chose to reproduce it originally was to largely fill a room with corpses, let them rot almost all the way, then summon several hiding monsters.  After the corpses rot away, the monsters are still hidden.

As bcode noted, this can also happen when the player is polymorphed into a hiding form.

The fix is in rot_corpse() in dig.c, which in GruntHack now checks to see if the player (or a monster) is at that location and if they're hiding under the corpse, and unhides them if so.


